## list_push, not binds = binds + — PASS

`tc_names.oo:27` `let mut binds: List[String] = list_new();`
Seven append sites, all `list_push`:

  :55  fname + "@0"
  :84  vname + "@" + ds
  :102 name + "@" + ds
  :121 name + "@" + ds
  :130 name + "@" + ds
  :148 name + "@" + ds
  :155 name + "@" + ds

Ripgrep `binds = binds` in `tc_names.oo` + `tc_scope.oo`: **zero**.
`name + "@" + ds` is per-entry payload, not whole-binds concat.

Out of B8: `check_scan.oo:178,187` still `binds = binds + cur + "@0\t"`
inside `names_to_depth0_binds`. Extra_binds String builder. Not the
typecheck List walk. Same leftover sprint11 named.

## drop_depth uses list_filter? — FAIL (it does not)

`tc_scope.oo:36-51` is an inlined while. Keep test is `!str_ends_with(e, marker)`.
Then `out = list_push(out, e)`. No call to `list_filter`.

Ripgrep `list_filter` under `ooda/`: one hit, `RELEASE_NOTES_v0.184.4-alpha.oot:12`
(`rewritten as list_filter`). Product code: **none**.

`scope_has` (`tc_scope.oo:19-34`) compares `name + "@" + d.to_string()`
to `list_get(binds, i)`. Exact `name@d`. Pass.

sprint11 said PASS on list_push, NOTE on list_filter wording, live
`str_ends_with`. That NOTE is the honest read. The **name** `list_filter`
is still false on SPRINT Task 11 request line 85 and in RELEASE_NOTES.

`b8_root_cause.oot:117` still talks about `let _drop = 0;` at
`tc_scope.oo:65` and a "list-filter branch". Live `tc_scope.oo` has
